# This model declares its OWN evaluation-point coordinates as parameterized
# params (`theta1`/`theta2` = elementof(reals)), so the ABI reuses those
# bindings directly instead of shadowing them with `t_`-prefixed duplicates.
# `inputs` is authoritative and exhaustive: duplicates would strand the
# model's own params with no argument slot, which is ill-formed.
inputs = (theta1, theta2)
outputs = logdensityof(posterior, record(theta1 = theta1, theta2 = theta2))
